@title Cooling advice: after adding a pair, the 3D run is put next to the 2D prediction
@area 3D
@sizes 1366x768 1920x1080
# The hot cabinet in 3D. Cooling advice finds a pair in the 2D model; Add puts it in Vents and fans and the Heat run goes again (Quick, coarse). When that 3D result is current the advice window adds a "Model comparison" block: per device the 2D prediction, the 3D result and the gap, labelled as two models and not a measurement. The picture is the evidence; the numbers are model numbers.
open qa/fixtures/cabinet-cooling-advice.novo
wait 20
click_text 3D #1
wait 30
click_text Heat #1
wait 20
# Opening Heat starts an automatic run: stop it, switch Auto off so it does not restart, and stop again.
click_text Cancel
wait 10
click_text Auto #1
wait 10
wait 30
try click_text Cancel
wait 30
try click_text Cancel
wait 30
try click_text Cancel
wait 30
click_text "Settings for the next run"
wait 10
click_text Quick
wait 10
click_text Simulate #2
wait_s 60
click_text "Cooling advice"
wait_s 90
expect "Tightest margin"
# At 1366 the advice window is as tall as its dock slot and the Add button is below its fold: scroll the list (just far enough for the winner's button, not to the last candidate; over the dock at 1366, over the 3D view at 1920 where it only zooms a little).
scroll 1200 300 -250
wait 6
click_text "Add these two to Vents and fans"
wait 10
expect "Added"
shot added-before-3d-result
# Auto is off, so the 3D run does not go again by itself: run it (Quick, as set above).
click_text Simulate #2
wait_s 400
# Back to the top of the advice list, where the comparison block sits.
scroll 1200 300 900
wait 6
expect "Model comparison"
expect "not a measurement"
shot comparison
check_layout
check_blank comparison
